---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Summary from '../components/Summary.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
---
<Base title={"Family Counseling in Provo & Utah | Tangible Therapy"} description={"Family Counseling at Tangible Mental Health: Reconnect, improve communication & resolve conflict in Provo & Orem, Utah. Safe space for parents, and teens. Book now!"}>
<section class="sec t-bright h-medium has-bg has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-bg"><img src="/images/tangible-42-9105a4.jpg" alt="" style="object-position:25% 34%" loading="eager"><div class="sec-ov" style="opacity:0.42"></div></div><div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:7;--mrows:10">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/5/6/23;--m:1/2/7/10"><div class="rte"><h1 class="ta-center">Family Counseling</h1><p class="lg ta-center">Family counseling that helps you reconnect and grow together</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:6/10/8/18;--m:8/2/10/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-medium btn-full" href="/contact">Start Family Counseling Today</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#fff" /></section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:19">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/6/12;--m:2/2/4/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2>When family life feels like too much</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/16/12/26;--m:12/2/19/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/tangible-50-acfccb.jpg" alt="A family of 3 sits on a large green couch inside a therapy office while a therapist conducts family therapy at Tangible Therapy" width="2500" height="1441" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:6/2/12/12;--m:4/2/12/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>Even the closest families struggle. Arguments repeat, boundaries blur, and emotions get misunderstood or ignored. Whether it’s parenting tension, sibling conflict, or generational stress, unresolved dynamics can leave everyone feeling frustrated, unheard, or emotionally distant.</p><p>Family therapy gives each member space to speak, listen, and rebuild connection with the guidance of a trained therapist, without blame or taking sides. </p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:14;--mrows:20">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/2/14/13;--m:13/2/20/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/tangible-51-e0ff2f.jpg" alt="A divorced couple sits across from one another in a therapy office while a female therapist sits in between and conducts therapy" width="3300" height="2550" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/15/4/26;--m:2/2/5/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>What family therapy helps with</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:4/15/15/25;--m:5/2/13/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>At Tangible Therapy, we help families work through:</p><ul><li><p>Parent/child or teen conflict</p></li><li><p>Communication breakdowns</p></li><li><p>Sibling tension or rivalry</p></li><li><p>Co-parenting after separation or divorce</p></li><li><p>Major life transitions or loss</p></li><li><p>Blended family adjustment</p></li><li><p>Generational trauma or cultural tension</p></li><li><p>Emotional disconnection or avoidance</p></li></ul><p>You don’t need to be in crisis to benefit from therapy. It is a proactive way to create healthier patterns and deepen relationships.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-white-bold h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:10;--mrows:18">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/2/4/11;--m:1/2/3/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>You’re not failing. You’re human.</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:1/14/11/25;--m:9/2/16/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/tangible-43-7b16a1.jpg" alt="A family sits in a brightly lit therapy office at Tangible Therapy while a therapist conducts a family therapy session." width="2500" height="1932" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:4/2/8/11;--m:3/2/10/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p><span class="c-accent">All families face challenges. The goal of therapy isn’t perfection, it’s connection. We’re here to help you move forward together, with more understanding, more peace, and more tools to support each other along the way.</span></p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:8/2/10/8;--m:16/2/18/10;--dz:5;--mz:5"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-medium btn-full" href="/contact">Book Your First Family Session</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-light h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:16;--mrows:7">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/7/3/22;--m:1/2/3/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">Family Therapists</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-summary-v2" style="--d:3/5/17/24;--m:3/2/8/10"><Summary kind="team" design="carousel" category="telehealth/couples,telehealth/teens" limit={9} perRow={3} rounded /></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-in" style="padding-top:1vmax;padding-bottom:0vmax">
<div class="wrap"><div class="list-title rte"><p>What you’ll get</p></div><ul class="ulist ulist-carousel" style="--per:3;--ar:3/2;--tfs:calc((2.2 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--bfs:calc((1.2 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--cw:75%;--gap:20px"><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="#" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Communicate more clearly and calmly</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Understand each other’s perspectives and emotional needs</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Navigate conflict with less defensiveness and more empathy</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Set healthy boundaries without guilt or confusion</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Rebuild trust, connection, and shared values</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="/" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>New insights into your relationship and communication patterns</p></div></div></li></ul><div class="carousel-nav"><button class="prev" aria-label="Previous"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19 12H5m6-6-6 6 6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button><button class="next" aria-label="Next"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button></div></div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#acb9ac" /></section>

<section class="sec t-black h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:20">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/4/26;--m:1/2/4/10"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">✺ Frequently asked questions ✺</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/2/14/13;--m:5/2/13/10"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>Do all family members have to attend every session?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Not necessarily. Depending on the situation, sessions may include everyone, certain subgroups (like parents and teens), or individual members. We’ll work with you to decide what structure is most helpful.</p></div></details><details><summary>What if someone in the family doesn’t want to participate?</summary><div class="rte"><p>That’s common, especially at the beginning. We’ll never force anyone, but we can start with those who are open and build trust over time. Sometimes, change begins with one person.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is this therapy for families in crisis only?</summary><div class="rte"><p>No. Many families use therapy to strengthen connections or improve communication — even if nothing major has happened. It's never too early to start.</p></div></details></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/15/10/26;--m:13/2/21/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>What ages do you work with in family therapy?</summary><div class="rte"><p>We typically work with families that include children 10 and up, but depending on the issue, we may also support younger children or recommend additional services.</p></div></details><details><summary>Will you take sides or tell us who’s “right”?</summary><div class="rte"><p>No. Our role is to support the system, not assign blame. We help each person feel heard and help the family as a whole develop more supportive ways of relating.</p></div></details></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</Base>
